Stage: BE

Purpose:
  Backend stage. Owns server-side implementation of the unit of work —
  business logic, persistence access, internal services — everything
  the API stage needs already working before it can expose a contract
  on top of it.


Requires:
  DB (only when the unit of work includes a data-layer change — see
  chains.sdd -> Dependency -> optional)


Produces:
  Working backend implementation that API can build a contract on top
  of.


Blocks:
  API — API MUST NOT execute until BE is DONE (see chains.sdd -> Rules
  [C5]).


Optional:
  This stage is skipped (never silently — see chains.sdd -> Rules [C7])
  only when the unit of work has no server-side change at all — rare in
  practice, since API almost always requires BE (see chains.sdd ->
  MobileExample).


Skills:
  @../../skills/backend/

  (see chains.sdd -> DoesNotOwn — this file defines WHEN/responsibility
  only; HOW the backend change is actually implemented belongs to
  skills/backend/, not here.)


State: + (vocabulary defined here; skills/backend/ content is not yet
  written — see skills/skills.sdd -> SkillDomains, state: boş)


Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Extracted out of the flat feature.chain /
  bugfix.chain / change.chain, where the BE responsibility was repeated
  inline in each file. Defined once here per NoDuplication; referenced
  from chains.sdd -> Stages and from every template under ./templates/
  that includes a BE step.
